quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  70,40,"So I swear by the Lord of all horizons of sunrise and all horizons of sunset that We are Capable,"
  70,41,of replacing them with others better than them. And We cannot be prevented (from doing so).
  70,42,"So leave them occupied with idle talk and to amuse (themselves) until they encounter their Day, which they have been promised (as Retribution),"
  70,43,"the Day they come out of the graves, hastening, as if racing towards a goal."
  70,44,Their (shameful) eyes will be downcast (and) disgrace will overtake them. That is the Day they have been promised.
  71,1,"Indeed, We sent Nuh (Noah) to his people, (saying:) ‘Warn your people before a painful punishment overtakes them.’"
  71,2,He said: ‘O my people! I am a clear warner to you.
  71,3,"Worship Allah, fear Him and obey me."
  71,4,"He will forgive your sins and grant you respite until an appointed time. Indeed, when Allah’s (appointed) time comes, it cannot be deferred if only you knew.’"
  71,5,"He said: ‘My Lord! Indeed, I have called my people night and day,"
  71,6,but my calling has only increased them in fleeing further away.
  71,7,"Every time I call them (towards faith) so that You may forgive them, they put their fingers in their ears, cover their heads with their garments, persist (in their disbelief) and act more proudly in their arrogance."
  71,8,"Then I called them openly,"
  71,9,and (again) appealed to them publicly and confided with them secretly.
  71,10,"I said (to them): ‘Seek forgiveness of your Lord. Indeed, He is Most-Forgiving."
